<Layout title="The Cost of Reactive Operations | PresciaIQ Insights"
  description="The Cost of Reactive Operations explores the hidden cost Australian businesses pay for lagging indicators. Discover how predictive AI eliminates latency.">
  <article class="pt-28 pb-20 px-4 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <a href="/insights/" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground mb-8 inline-block">← Back to Insights</a>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8">
      <span class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest bg-card border border-border px-3 py-1 rounded-full uppercase">Issue 01</span>
      <span class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">April 2026</span>
      <span class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">8 min read</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold mb-4">The Cost of <span class="text-[#00ff88]">Reactive</span> Operations</h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-muted-foreground mb-12">Why Most Australian Businesses Are Paying for Lagging Indicators</p>
    <p class="text-lg mb-6"><span class="float-left text-7xl font-bold leading-none mr-3 mt-1">T</span>here's a cost most businesses never put on the balance sheet. Call it operational drag — the price of reactive decisions. It's what you pay every time you find out about something after it's already happened.</p>
    <p class="mb-6">It's the two weeks of ad spend you burned before realising the campaign was dead. The crew you sent to a job that wasn't ready. The build that slipped six weeks because nobody clocked the supplier delay forming.</p>
    <p class="mb-12">None of these get filed under "we were too slow." They get booked as marketing costs, labour, write-offs, bad luck. Which is exactly why operational latency is so brutal. Nobody's measuring it, so nobody's fighting it.</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Reactive doesn't mean lazy. It means blind.</h2>
    <p class="mb-6">The instinct is to blame execution. It's almost never an execution problem.</p>
    <p class="mb-12">The businesses paying the highest operational latency are usually the ones grinding the hardest. Dashboards everywhere. Weekly standups. Someone refreshing reports at 7am. Problem is, every one of those tools is pointed at yesterday.</p>
    <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[#00ff88] pl-6 py-2 my-8 text-xl italic">What's about to happen, and what should I do about it before it does?</blockquote>
    <p class="mb-12">If your tools can't answer that, you don't have an intelligence stack. You have a filing system with charts on it.</p>
